  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to AU on accelerating  the implimentation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Union&#x2019;s Office of the Special Envoy on Women Peace and Security (AU OSE-WPS), established in 2014, leads efforts to advance the WPS agenda within the African Continent. It has helped initiate measures and continenetal frameworks to advance women&#x2019;s inclusion in peace and political process in line with the four pillars of WPS: participation, prevention, protection and relief and recovery. The AU OSE-WPS is also a key player in the adoption of National Action Plans, now adopted by 37 Member States.</narrative>
  </description>
